Count occurrences of a number in a sorted array with duplicates
Given a sorted array, arr[] and a number target, you need to find the number of occurrences of target in arr[]. 

Explanation:

Find the first and last index of the target in the array. then (last_pos - first_pos + 1) is the total number of target elements count.

Code:
class Solution {
    int countFreq(int[] arr, int target) {
        // code here
        int n=arr.length;
        int left=0; int right=n-1;
        int count=0; 
        int[] ans={-1,-1};
        
        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;
            if(arr[mid]==target){
                ans[0]=mid;
                right=mid-1;
            }
            else if(arr[mid]<target){
                left=mid+1;
            }
            else if(arr[mid]>target){
                right=mid-1;
            }
        }
        
        left=0; right=n-1;
        
        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;
            if(arr[mid]==target){
                ans[1]=mid;
                left=mid+1;
            }
            else if (arr[mid]<target){
                left=mid+1;
            }
            else if(arr[mid]>target){
                right=mid-1;
            }
        }
        
        if(ans[0]==-1){
            return 0;
        }
        
        count=ans[1]-ans[0]+1;
        return count;
    }
}
